## Criteria and verdicts

{% set planning_unit_split_allowed = true %}
{% include 'shared/_criterion_verification_procedure.j2' %}

Use one stable `PA-###` item per criterion in `## Criterion Verdicts`.
Include `Plan-level:` or a plan reference — `Step: [S-n]` when the plan
numbers its steps, or a `Plan reference: [<stable id>]` when it does not —
then `Criterion:`, `Expected observation:`, `Observation:`,
`Proposed revision:`, `Verdict:`, `Evidence:`, `Location:`, and `Cost:`.
`completed` requires every criterion to be `met` with evidence and no
counterexample found; a completed decision does not need a revision because
the plan was approved as-is. For `request_changes` or `failed`, every
criterion verdict carries a `Proposed revision:` (write `none` for a met
criterion), and each localized non-met verdict is mirrored in
`## What Came Up Short` with its revision so the planner can apply or rebut
it. `Proposed revision:` is enforced on submission for non-completed
decisions (`ANALYSIS019`). Do not add `How To Fix`. A `not evaluable`
criterion requires `failed`.

